UID:pulitzer-center-global-south-civil-society-microgrants-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pulitzer Center: Global South Civil Society Microgrants 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Pulitzer Center funds civil society in the Global South to 
 build civic engagement projects around Pulitzer Center-supported journalis
 m: grassroots collectives\, community-led movements\, ARTISTS and civic co
 alitions taking published reporting to the communities it concerns. This g
 rant cycle is restricted to the Center's Climate and Environment topics: R
 AINFOREST (drivers of rainforest degradation\, the role of global markets\
 , finance and policy\, centring the rights and roles of Indigenous peoples
 )\, OCEAN (degradation of marine environments\, ocean health and the clima
 te crisis\, ocean governance\, science-backed and community-led solutions)
 \, and CLIMATE AND LABOR (the intersection of climate and labour\, includi
 ng gender\, livelihoods\, adaptation and community resilience). WHAT COUNT
 S AS A PROJECT: community engagement and organising that connects reportin
 g with audiences\; creative expressions\, explicitly including digital cam
 paigns\, public performances and creative publication formats\; public dia
 logues bringing together affected communities\, journalists\, decision-mak
 ers and academia\; and other innovative uses of the reporting that build o
 n local cultural practices. Every project must use at least one published 
 Pulitzer Center-supported reporting project meaningfully\, or involve a Pu
 litzer Center-supported journalist centrally\, and must name a clear targe
 t audience. OUT OF SCOPE: journalism and reporting projects themselves (th
 ose go to the Center's reporting grants)\, anything not built on Pulitzer 
 Center-supported reporting\, direct advocacy or lobbying\, campaigns endor
 sing political candidates or parties\, and for-profit projects. WHO CAN AP
 PLY: grassroots organisations\, community educators\, civil society organi
 sations and coalitions\, youth movements and other groups working at the i
 ntersection of journalism\, civic rights and active citizenship\, with pas
 t experience running civic engagement activities in the Global South\, pro
 ven experience on the named topics\, and the operational capacity to manag
 e a microgrant from an international organisation. APPLICATION: a project 
 description of no more than 400 words\, the target audience and desired im
 pact\, your methodology\, a timeline and budget\, the lead applicant's CV 
 with a letter of recommendation\, and\, where activities involve Indigenou
 s peoples or traditional communities\, a signed or recorded statement of c
 onsent from a community member. Applications are accepted in English\, Spa
 nish\, Portuguese\, French and Indonesian through Submittable. TIMELINE: a
 pplications 15 August to 6 September 2026\, selection announced mid-Septem
 ber 2026\, onboarding October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pulitzer Center\nLoca
 tion: Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and South
 east Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. Ci
 vil Society Microgrant instead.\nAward: USD 2\,000 to USD 4\,000 per proje
 ct. Applicants name the amount requested and submit a draft budget. Funds 
 are transferred to the partner after the agreement is signed\; partners fi
 le a financial narrative and outcomes report at the end but are NOT requir
 ed to collect detailed receipts. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to six 
 months of implementation\, October 2026 to March 2027\, with a virtual che
 ck-in in December 2026 and closure in early March 2027.\n\nMore: https://p
 ulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/global-south-
 civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://pulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/g
 lobal-south-civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and Sou
 theast Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. 
 Civil Society Microgrant instead.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:instituto-sacatar-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: Instituto Sacatar: Sacatar Fellowship 2027 (Bahia\, Brazi
 l)
DESCRIPTION:Brazil's longest-running artist residency\, on the island of It
 aparica across the bay from Salvador\, hosting six to eight artists per se
 ssion for roughly eight weeks. Open to all creative disciplines and\, unus
 ually for this region\, to all nationalities\, which makes it one of the f
 ew genuinely international residencies in Latin America. Sacatar provides 
 full hosting (private room\, three meals daily\, individual studio\, laund
 ry\, local logistics and connections) but explicitly does NOT provide a st
 ipend\, airfare to Salvador\, art materials or discretionary local expense
 s\, so applicants must fund their own travel. Individual artists only\; gr
 oup proposals are not accepted and former Sacatar Fellows may not reapply.
  COVID vaccination is required. NOTE: there is a USD 25 application fee. A
 pply through SlideRoom by 28 August 2026. Contact info@sacatar.org.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Instituto Sacatar\nLocation: Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil.
  Open to all nationalities.\nAward: Fully hosted residency: private bedroo
 m with attached bathroom\, three meals a day (except Saturday evenings\, S
 undays and Brazilian holidays)\, an individual studio suited to the discip
 line\, weekly laundry\, logistical support and airport transfer from Salva
 dor. NO STIPEND\, no airfare and no materials budget. USD 25 application f
 ee. One French artist may additionally receive airfare and a stipend throu
 gh Villa Fatumbi.\nDuration: Approximately eight weeks\; specific session 
 dates are listed in the application.\n\nMore: https://sacatar.org/en/fello
 wships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sacatar.org/en/fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil. Open to all nationalities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:human-rights-watch-ai-strategy-solutions-lead-2026@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Human Rights Watch: AI Strategy and Solutions Lead (one-y
 ear fixed term)
DESCRIPTION:Human Rights Watch is hiring an AI Strategy and Solutions Lead 
 into its Operations Department to build the foundation for responsible AI 
 adoption across the organisation. The role deliberately sits between strat
 egy and execution: assessing organisational readiness\, mapping partnershi
 ps and governance\, and also prototyping and shipping working systems. THE
  WORK\, in four strands. (1) STRATEGY AND READINESS: with the CIO and the 
 Information Security and Technology (IST) leadership team\, build an AI st
 rategy covering data foundation requirements\, infrastructure gaps and org
 anisational readiness\; assess current state and shape a roadmap balancing
  quick wins against long-term capacity\; research what peer nonprofit\, hu
 manitarian and human rights organisations are doing and find collaboration
  openings. (2) FLAGSHIP SOLUTIONS: work with departments to find high-impa
 ct use cases\, translate business needs into technical approaches\, build 
 and deploy AI/ML solutions with measurable value (time saved\, efficiency\
 , better outcomes)\, using the Microsoft AI ecosystem (Copilot Studio\, Az
 ure AI\, Power Platform) among other tools\, and oversee consultants and v
 endors to extend delivery capacity. (3) ADOPTION AND CAPACITY: balance onb
 oarding staff onto AI tools against building custom solutions where they a
 mplify the organisation's strengths\; write training material pitched at d
 ifferent work areas and skill levels covering prompting and responsible us
 e\; support working groups and communities of practice\; produce playbooks
  and guides for non-technical staff. (4) GOVERNANCE: partner with IST lead
 ership on risk assessment frameworks\, align solutions with security\, inf
 rastructure and architecture requirements\, contribute to AI policy develo
 pment and its operationalisation\, set standards for evaluating proofs of 
 concept and MVPs\, and engage business units so outcomes are co-owned\; al
 l of it balanced against data quality\, security and resource constraints 
 and HRW's mission as a human rights organisation. WHO THEY WANT: a bachelo
 r's degree or equivalent work experience in computer science\, data scienc
 e\, information systems\, mathematics\, AI/ML implementation or a related 
 technical field\; a minimum of seven years' relevant experience including 
 two to three years on AI and two to three years implementing AI/ML in prod
 uction\; experience contributing to technology strategy and assessing orga
 nisational readiness for new technology\; strong Python and ML library/fra
 mework skills\; hands-on predictive modelling\, data science and statistic
 al analysis\; experience with low-code/no-code AI platforms such as Copilo
 t Studio or Power Platform\; a track record of scoping and delivering unde
 r resource constraints\; a grasp of both generative AI and traditional ML\
 ; and the ability to explain technical concepts plainly to mixed audiences
 \, engage stakeholders and lead technology adoption as an internal partner
  to business teams. PREFERRED: nonprofit\, humanitarian or human rights ex
 perience\; data privacy\, security and ethical AI knowledge\; familiarity 
 with responsible AI frameworks and governance models\; vendor and consulta
 nt management\; and a background in politically sensitive or high-risk env
 ironments. APPLY: through the HRW job portal with a cover letter and CV\, 
 preferably as PDFs\, by 30 August 2026. Only complete applications are rev
 iewed and only shortlisted candidates are contacted\; no calls or email en
 quiries. HRW states that it does not discriminate on the basis of disabili
 ty\, age\, gender identity and expression\, national origin\, race and eth
 nicity\, religious beliefs\, sexual orientation or criminal record.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Human Rights Watch (HRW)\, Operations Department\nLocation: Mus
 t be within commuting distance of an HRW office: Amsterdam\, Amman\, Berli
 n\, Brussels\, London\, Stockholm\, New York\, Washington DC\, Miami\, Sao
  Paulo\, Toronto or Chicago. Reports to the Chief Information Officer in B
 erlin. No relocation support and no work-authorisation sponsorship.\nAward
 : USD 102\,000 to 112\,000 plus employer-paid benefits if based in the US\
 ; ranges outside the US are set by local market conditions. No application
  fee.\nDuration: One year fixed-term\, full time. Application deadline 30 
 August 2026.\n\nMore: https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/humanrightswatch/jo
 bs/8350654002?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/humanrightswatch/jobs/8350654002?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Must be within commuting distance of an HRW office: Amsterdam\, Am
 man\, Berlin\, Brussels\, London\, Stockholm\, New York\, Washington DC\, 
 Miami\, Sao Paulo\, Toronto or Chicago. Reports to the Chief Information O
 fficer in Berlin. No relocation support and no work-authorisation sponsors
 hip.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tilting-axis-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tilting Axis Fellowship 2027 for Caribbean-Based Practiti
 oners (with Nieuwe Instituut)
DESCRIPTION:The Tilting Axis Fellowship 2027 supports researchers\, designe
 rs\, writers\, curators and cultural producers based in the Caribbean regi
 on\, led by Nieuwe Instituut with Stedelijk Museum Amsterdam\, Fresh Milk 
 (Barbados)\, RAA! (Aruba) and Instituto Buena Bista (Curacao). Formal degr
 ees are not required\; the program prioritises creativity\, critical think
 ing and strong potential over credentials. FUNDING: a EUR 2\,500 stipend p
 er fellow\, up to EUR 1\,000 additional travel budget for research-related
  movement within or beyond the Caribbean\, and full coverage of airfare an
 d programming for the Netherlands visit. PROGRAM: six weeks in April-May 2
 027 with weekly check-ins and a self-defined project milestone\, including
  a 10-day visit to the Netherlands with five days of tailored cultural pro
 gramming\, site visits and meetings with artists and institutions. ELIGIBI
 LITY: residents of designated Caribbean territories (including Cuba\, Jama
 ica\, Haiti\, Trinidad and Tobago and others)\; diaspora members based els
 ewhere are not eligible. APPLY: proposals by email to ta-fellowship@nieuwe
 instituut.nl. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Tilting Axis\, w
 ith Nieuwe Instituut\, Stedelijk Museum Amsterdam\, Fresh Milk (Barbados)\
 , RAA! (Aruba) and Instituto Buena Bista (Curacao)\nLocation: Caribbean-ba
 sed (applicants must be residents of designated Caribbean territories\; di
 aspora not eligible). Six-week program with a 10-day visit to the Netherla
 nds\, airfare and programming covered.\nAward: EUR 2\,500 stipend per fell
 ow\, plus up to EUR 1\,000 travel budget for research-related movement and
  full coverage of airfare and Netherlands programming during the visit. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Six weeks\, April-May 2027\, including a 10-d
 ay Netherlands visit with five days of tailored cultural programming.\n\nM
 ore: https://tiltingaxis.org/news/ta-fellowship-2027?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tiltingaxis.org/news/ta-fellowship-2027?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Caribbean-based (applicants must be residents of designated Caribb
 ean territories\; diaspora not eligible). Six-week program with a 10-day v
 isit to the Netherlands\, airfare and programming covered.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:la-nueva-fabrica-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Deadline: La Nueva Fabrica Residency 2027-2028 (Antigua\, Guatemala
 )
DESCRIPTION:La Nueva Fabrica (LNF)\, a nonprofit contemporary art space in 
 Antigua\, Guatemala\, invites applications for its 2027-2028 residency. Th
 e residency is research-focused rather than production-focused: no final a
 rtwork is required\, and residents are supported in developing their pract
 ice in dialogue with the local context. FUNDING: a USD 2\,000 stipend\, fr
 ee housing in an equipped house on-site\, airport transfers from Guatemala
  City's La Aurora International Airport\, curatorial and logistical suppor
 t\, and access to community programming\; travel to Guatemala is the resid
 ent's own responsibility. ELIGIBILITY: open to people 18 and over of any n
 ationality\, with no formal academic requirements\; applicants should demo
 nstrate a direct connection to LNF's context and genuine interest in commu
 nity engagement. Duo applications are accepted\; five residents are select
 ed annually by an independent jury\, with finalist interviews via Zoom on 
 16 December 2026 and results announced 18 January 2027. STAY: 4-8 weeks be
 tween 1 September 2027 and 30 June 2028. APPLY: online form\, in English o
 r Spanish. DEADLINE: 18 October 2026\, 6:00 PM Guatemala time.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: La Nueva Fabrica (LNF)\nLocation: Antigua\, Guatemala. Open to appli
 cants 18+ of any nationality\; international and domestic travel to LNF is
  the resident's own responsibility (airport transfers from La Aurora Inter
 national Airport are covered).\nAward: USD 2\,000 stipend\, plus free hous
 ing in an equipped on-site house\, airport transfers\, curatorial and logi
 stical support\, and access to community programming. Five residents selec
 ted annually. No application fee.\nDuration: 4-8 weeks\, coordinated with 
 LNF\, between 1 September 2027 and 30 June 2028.\n\nMore: https://lanuevaf
 abrica.org/es/residencia/convocatorias/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lanuevafabrica.org/es/residencia/convocatorias/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Antigua\, Guatemala. Open to applicants 18+ of any nationality\; i
 nternational and domestic travel to LNF is the resident's own responsibili
 ty (airport transfers from La Aurora International Airport are covered).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-suriname-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Suriname 2027 (Par
 amaribo\, Moengo\, Frederiksdorp)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or interdisciplinary maker f
 or a three-month residency in 2027 across three locations in Suriname: Par
 amaribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp\, each with its own cultural\, historic
 al and social context. The residency is inspired by the Surinamese notion 
 of alakondre (literally 'all countries')\, which symbolises living togethe
 r in cultural diversity and emphasises the power of coexisting differences
 . Rather than simply promoting harmony\, alakondre acknowledges historical
  inequalities\, cultural sensitivities and tensions ensuing from colonial 
 and socio-economic realities\, which demands openness and critical awarene
 ss of your position as a creative practitioner\; personal stories\, whethe
 r family history or questions of identity\, can provide powerful entry poi
 nts. A network of local partners supports the residency\, and at each loca
 tion a local maker selected by Surinamese partner organisations works alon
 gside you\, creating natural opportunities for creative exchange and dialo
 gue. ELIGIBILITY: you are an individual designer\, architect or spatial pr
 actitioner\; you are established in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (the Ne
 therlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maar
 ten)\; you are registered in the register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce
  (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\
 ; and you have run a professional practice within the creative industries 
 for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or collaborative p
 artnerships\, nor to current recipients of the Talent Development Grant Sc
 heme\, the Open Call Self-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design
  Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this open call means you cannot apply to tho
 se schemes and open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for the thr
 ee-month residency\; one position is awarded. Assessment takes the form of
  a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the artistic 
 quality of the work\, the quality of the development plan and the motivati
 on in relation to the residency's objective\, and the highest-scoring prop
 osal is awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing date. Submit v
 ia the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund
  NL) with local partner organisations in Suriname\nLocation: Residency tak
 es place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\, Moengo and Frederiks
 dorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\
 , Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherla
 nds) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Nethe
 rlands.\nAward: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for a three-month residency\, paid by t
 he Creative Industries Fund NL. One residency position is awarded. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Three months in 2027\, moving between Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-residency-suriname?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-suriname
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlan
 ds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Ki
 ngdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the
  Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salta-art-ebenboeckhaus-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Salta art / AIR-M Ebenböckhaus Residency 2027 for South 
 American Artists (Munich)
DESCRIPTION:AIR-M Ebenböckhaus and the non-profit Salta art\, in partnersh
 ip with ERA Foundation\, offer a residency for two contemporary visual art
 ists from South America at the Ebenböckhaus in Munich-Pasing\, Germany\, 
 from 7 July to 29 September 2027. Since 2022 the Department of Arts and Cu
 lture of the City of Munich has collaborated with Salta art to extend the 
 residency programme to South America\; ERA Foundation's support funds the 
 second position. WHAT YOU GET: a grant and accommodation contract of EUR 1
 \,300 per month from the City of Munich\, rent-free accommodation in a sha
 red apartment with individual lockable rooms\, three work and presentation
  rooms (52 m2) in the house\, return tickets from South America (economy /
  2nd class)\, a shared studio at Empfangshalle in the Museumsquartier\, a 
 EUR 600 research trip allowance and a MakerPlus membership at MakerSpace M
 unich (wood\, metal\, electronics\, IoT\, laser cutting\, additive manufac
 turing\, textile workshops). A mentoring initiative pairs each resident wi
 th a Munich-based curator for up to three meetings\, a research trip is or
 ganised\, and an Open Studio event closes the residency. A curator from So
 uth America will also live and work at the house for part of the period. E
 LIGIBILITY: professional visual artists (painting\, drawing\, sculpture\, 
 photography\, film\, video\, digital art\, performance or interdisciplinar
 y practices) born and based or residing in South America\, over 18\, not s
 tudents\, who pursue art as their main occupation and can demonstrate prof
 essional experience\; former residents of Villa Waldberta or Ebenböckhaus
  are not eligible. A good level of spoken English is required and applicat
 ions must be completed in English. APPLICATION: free\, via Google Form wit
 h one PDF (max 10MB\, 20 pages) containing personal information\, one refe
 ree contact\, a 200-word biography\, CV (max 4 pages)\, letter of intent\,
  practice description (max 500 words) and work samples. Selection is decid
 ed by the City of Munich on the recommendation of the Salta art jury (Aman
 da Carneiro\, MASP\; Chus Martinez\; Anna Schneider\, DAS MINSK)\; outcome
 s by end of December 2026. Note: the Ebenböckhaus is not barrier-free. DE
 ADLINE: 15 November 2026\, midnight CET.\n\nOrganisation: Salta art with A
 IR-M Ebenböckhaus (City of Munich) and ERA Foundation\nLocation: Ebenböc
 khaus\, Munich-Pasing\, Germany. Open only to visual artists born and base
 d or residing in South America.\nAward: Grant and accommodation contract o
 f EUR 1\,300 per month per artist from the City of Munich (accommodation i
 s rent-free)\, plus return travel from South America (economy / 2nd class)
 \, a shared studio at Empfangshalle in Munich's Museumsquartier\, a EUR 60
 0 research trip allowance and a MakerPlus membership at MakerSpace Munich.
  No application fee.\nDuration: 7 July to 29 September 2027 (about 12 week
 s\, 2 positions).\n\nMore: https://saltaart.org/application?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://saltaart.org/application?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ebenböckhaus\, Munich-Pasing\, Germany. Open only to visual artis
 ts born and based or residing in South America.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:big-festival-gamescom-latam-2027-indie-submissions@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090226Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Deadline: BIG Festival at gamescom latam 2027: free indie game subm
 issions (Sao Paulo\, awards with cash prizes)
DESCRIPTION:BIG Festival\, the indie games competition inside gamescom lata
 m in Sao Paulo\, has opened free submissions for its 2027 edition. The 202
 6 edition drew a record 966 submissions from 75 countries. WHO: independen
 t developers and studios anywhere in the world\, with a playable game or d
 emo\; see the official rules for category requirements (BIG Starter\, BIG 
 Highlight and the WINGS Award for teams where women and marginalised group
 s hold prominent roles). WHAT YOU GET: selected titles are exhibited at no
  cost on the show floor\, playtested by visitors\, and compete for the BIG
  Festival awards\; past editions paid cash to winners (BRL 5\,000 for Best
  Game 2025\, EUR 2\,000 for the 2026 WINGS Award). A separate free call fo
 r conference speakers closes 18 January 2027. APPLICATION: via the gamesco
 m latam website. DEADLINE: 15 January 2027 at 21:59 Eastern time.\n\nOrgan
 isation: gamescom latam / BIG Festival\nLocation: Sao Paulo\, Brazil (Dist
 rito Anhembi). Open to independent developers anywhere in the world.\nAwar
 d: Free submission and a no-cost exhibition slot for selected games\, plus
  eligibility for the BIG Festival awards. 2027 prize amounts are not yet p
 ublished\; in 2025 Best Game carried BRL 5\,000 and in 2026 the WINGS Awar
 d carried EUR 2\,000 in cash.\nDuration: Submissions 16 October 2026 to 15
  January 2027\; festival 22 to 25 April 2027.\n\nMore: https://latam.games
 com.global/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://latam.gamescom.global/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sao Paulo\, Brazil (Distrito Anhembi). Open to independent develop
 ers anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
